From c78a4aec7fad2097d54978e9823d87c81c41c1c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: go-while <go-while@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:10:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix const qualifiers discarded with C23 string functions

glibc 2.43 implements the C23 qualifier-preserving strchr, strrchr,
strstr, strpbrk, memchr and bsearch: called with a pointer to const,
they return a pointer to const.  gcc then warns for each assignment of
the result to a plain pointer (16 warnings on Ubuntu 26.04 with gcc 15
and glibc 2.43, 19 on Arch Linux with gcc 16 and glibc 2.44, which also
covers strstr).

Most pointers are only read and are now declared const.  Elsewhere:

- nnrpd wrote NUL bytes into the response returned by ARTpost(), which
  may be a string literal; it now replies with a copy of its first line.
- nnrpd removed the insecure SASL mechanisms from the list returned by
  sasl_listmech(), which belongs to the SASL library; it now works on a
  copy.
- archive cuts the group names in its own copy of the Xref header field
  body, as storage/ov.c does, with a cast.
- innd looks for the site exclusions in the writable newsfeeds entry
  rather than through the const site name, and NGparseentry() takes the
  writable active file line it stores pointers into.

The dbm_open() warning of ckpasswd is #299.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
